WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Your lens: why copied habits fade.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.230
It is two in the morning. Bima is finishing a report that is due at nine. Again.

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:17.530
He has tried the fixes: a planner, an app, an earlier alarm. Each one lasted about a week.

4
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:26.010
The fixes fail because they are practices. Think of three layers: practices are what you do, paradigms are the lens you see work through, and principles stay true whether you believe them or not.

5
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:31.760
So he audits the lens. What would I have to believe for all-night work to make sense? Only pressure makes me work.

6
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.140
Then he tests that belief against evidence. His two best pieces of work this year were both started early.

7
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:46.490
A new lens: a start I schedule beats a deadline I fear. The practices follow by themselves.

8
00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:54.850
Growth at work follows an order. You start directed. Then self-directed: you own your responses, your direction and your schedule. Only then are you trusted with others.

9
00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:00.990
Three weeks later. It is Monday afternoon, the report is due on Thursday, and it is already half done. He did not find a better app. He changed the lens.

10
00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:08.390
Practices copied without their lens fade in weeks. A changed lens changes many practices at once.

11
00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.190
Now it is your turn. Take your least effective habit and ask: what would I have to believe for this to make sense?
